--------------------------- MODULE PaymentReview ---------------------------
EXTENDS PaymentReviewData

\* Purpose and limits
\* A review slot is one optional case on a payment row that needs an owner's attention.
\* This model checks attempts to open, acknowledge, or end that case.
\* Held means the slot contains a case. It does not mean a worker holds a claim.
\* It does not model row settlement, database transactions, authorisation,
\* concurrent callers, or whether an operator eventually resolves a case.
\* Event declarations say that these operations do not move money.
\* The model checks that declaration. It does not inspect balances or transfers.
\*
\* Read the notation
\* MODULE names this set of rules. EXTENDS imports the names that it uses.
\* The final line of = signs ends the module.
\* == defines a rule. = compares values. \in means "belongs to".
\* A set lists possible values. A tuple is an ordered list of columns.
\* Square brackets select a tuple column, with 1 as the first column.
\* /\ and \/ mean "and" and "or". ~ means "not".
\* => means that the left condition requires the right condition.
\* \E chooses a value from a set that makes the following conditions true.
\* IF chooses between THEN and ELSE. CASE tests the listed alternatives.
\* [] starts another case. -> gives its result. OTHER is the fallback case.
\* A name without a final ' describes its value before a step.
\* A final ' marks its value after the step. UNCHANGED keeps the listed values.
\* BOOLEAN contains TRUE and FALSE. Str means a word. Bool means a truth value.
\* Equality states a condition. It is not a command to assign a value.
\* A step constrains the values before and after it at the same time.
\* The type notes are checked inputs to Apalache, not only reader guidance.
\*
\* Data from the code
\* A representative is a sample record for one declared state.
\* The proof trusts that those samples cover the real cases that matter.
\* PaymentReviewData is generated by scripts/verify-models/review.ts.
\* The generator runs each declared event on each representative review slot.
\* review-machine-spec.ts supplies those declarations and sample records.
\* Each call receives a clone of its sample, so later calls start from the same facts.
\* The declared reasons are partially_returned_obligation and shared_reference.
\* Each has an unseen and an acknowledged sample. A further sample has no case.
\*
\* ReviewStates contains the source and target labels observed in those
\* runs. The empty slot is "none". Held labels include the actual reason:
\* "open(reason)" means unseen and "seen(reason)" means acknowledged.
\* These names include state and reason, but not the actual case identifier.
\* Two cases can share a name without being the same case.
\*
\* ReviewNodes contains four-column tuples:
\*   1. The reason-refined label, or "none".
\*   2. Whether the slot holds a case.
\*   3. Whether acknowledgedAt is present on that case.
\*   4. The actual reason kind, or the empty string for an empty slot.
\* ReviewEvents contains four-column tuples:
\*   1. The event identifier used to join an attempt to its declaration.
\*   2. The action: "open", "acknowledge", or "retire".
\*   3. The reason suffix of an open or retire identifier. Acknowledgement
\*      uses the empty string because it is not specific to a reason.
\*   4. The declared movesMoney flag.
\* Each open event introduces its named reason. Each retire event names the reason it can remove.
\* In the code, partially_returned_obligation needs all_returned_and_recorded evidence.
\* shared_reference needs unique_reference evidence.
\* The model does not represent those evidence facts. Event names select the matching rule.
\* Direct tests must check that callers supply the right evidence.
\*
\* ReviewAttempts contains seven-column tuples:
\*   1. The observed source label.
\*   2. The attempted event identifier.
\*   3. The observed target label.
\*   4. The representative tag: "empty" or its reason kind. This records
\*      where the sample came from. The safety rule does not use this tag.
\*   5. Whether the call returned without an error.
\*   6. Whether the actual before and after caseId values are equal.
\*   7. Whether the actual before and after reason.kind values are equal.
\* These comparisons use the actual fields, not the simpler state-and-reason names.
\* A changed case identifier therefore cannot hide behind an unchanged name.
\* Two absent values compare equal. A new or removed case makes both comparisons false.
\* New and removed cases are allowed for open and retire events.
\*
\* The helper maps a thrown call to null. The generator records it as refused.
\* Its target comes from the cloned input, including any change before the error.
\* A normal return of undefined means an empty slot, not a refusal.
\* Retirement is accepted even though it returns no value.
\* A successful call that leaves its slot unchanged is still accepted.
\* These facts describe the finite representatives and declared events,
\* not all possible timestamps, identifiers, inputs, or external evidence.
\*
\* Model memory
\* review stores the current state-and-reason name, not a full case.
\* attemptsSafe records whether every attempt so far passed SafeAttempt.
\* Once an attempt makes this flag FALSE, later steps cannot repair it.

VARIABLES
  \* @type: Str;
  review,
  \* @type: Bool;
  attemptsSafe

\* TypeOK keeps the current label in the generated state set and the
\* history flag in the set of truth values.
TypeOK ==
  /\ review \in ReviewStates
  /\ attemptsSafe \in BOOLEAN

\* SafeAttempt judges an observed outcome. It does not enable the call.
\* Match the attempt's labels and event identifier to their generated
\* facts. Reject an event whose declaration says it moves money, whether
\* the attempt was accepted or refused.
\*
\* For an accepted call, any held-to-held outcome must preserve the actual
\* case identifier and reason kind, not merely their abstract labels.
\* Opening must start empty and finish with an unseen case of the event's
\* reason. This rejects a successful reopen, including a same-reason no-op.
\* Acknowledgement must start with an unseen case and leave it held and
\* seen. The held-to-held check also preserves its case and reason.
\* A second successful acknowledgement therefore fails this rule.
\* Retirement must start held, match the held reason, and finish empty.
\* Either an unseen or a seen case can retire. No accepted unknown action
\* is safe, because the final CASE branch is FALSE.
\*
\* For a refusal, require the same label, actual case identifier, and
\* actual reason kind. Only those recorded fields must stay unchanged.
\* The proof does not inspect other fields or external side effects of a refused call.
\* A refusal still takes a model step. An accepted no-op faces the accepted rules.
\* @type: (<<Str, Str, Str, Str, Bool, Bool, Bool>>) => Bool;
SafeAttempt(a) ==
  \E before \in ReviewNodes, after \in ReviewNodes, event \in ReviewEvents :
    /\ before[1] = a[1]
    /\ after[1] = a[3]
    /\ event[1] = a[2]
    /\ ~event[4]
    /\ IF a[5]
       THEN /\ ((before[2] /\ after[2]) => (a[6] /\ a[7]))
            /\ CASE event[2] = "open" ->
                      /\ ~before[2]
                      /\ after[2]
                      /\ ~after[3]
                      /\ after[4] = event[3]
                 [] event[2] = "acknowledge" ->
                      /\ before[2]
                      /\ ~before[3]
                      /\ after[2]
                      /\ after[3]
                 [] event[2] = "retire" ->
                      /\ before[2]
                      /\ before[4] = event[3]
                      /\ ~after[2]
                 [] OTHER -> FALSE
       ELSE /\ a[1] = a[3]
            /\ a[6]
            /\ a[7]

\* Safety checks
\* Safety combines well-formed memory with the claim that no unsafe
\* attempt has occurred. It adds no separate restriction on reachability.
Safety == TypeOK /\ attemptsSafe

\* Init starts with an empty review slot and no recorded failure.
Init ==
  /\ review = "none"
  /\ attemptsSafe = TRUE

\* ReviewStep can choose any generated attempt whose source matches the current review name.
\* It uses the recorded outcome even if that outcome is unsafe.
\* It does not require SafeAttempt before the step.
\* Thus accepted and refused attempts both remain visible to the checker.
\* The and condition retains each earlier failure and records a new failure.
\* Steps join by state-and-reason names, not by an actual case identifier.
\* The identity check compares the actual records before and after each generated call.
ReviewStep ==
  \E attempt \in ReviewAttempts :
    /\ attempt[1] = review
    /\ review' = attempt[3]
    /\ attemptsSafe' = (attemptsSafe /\ SafeAttempt(attempt))

\* Next also permits a step that changes nothing. A pause cannot clear the history flag.
\* No rule requires another attempt to occur.
Next == ReviewStep \/ UNCHANGED <<review, attemptsSafe>>

\* Proof checks
\* The runner checks Safety at Init with length zero.
\* It separately checks one Next step from every state that satisfies Safety.
\* This starting set is not limited to states that Init can reach.
\* For example, it includes each generated review name with a TRUE history flag.
\* The initial check and this unrestricted next-step check establish Safety for any finite run length.
\* This is not only a search through a short initial trace.
\* The conclusion covers these generated facts and model steps.
\* It does not promise that an operator will acknowledge or end a case.
InductionStart == Safety
=============================================================================
